## 3. What you're not allowed to do

When using, forking, modifying, or redistributing the Software (or any derivative of it), You must NOT:

- **a. Claim it as your own original work.** You must not represent the Software, or a modified version of it, as something You created from scratch. Where You did not create the original project, say so.
- **b. Redistribute a modified version without attribution.** Any redistribution of the Software, or a derivative/fork of it, must include:
  - A clear statement that it is based on / forked from Koi Dataset Forge,
  - The name "DMJ Labs" as the original Licensor,
  - A link to the original project (if publicly available),
  - A copy of this license.
- **c. Remove or obscure** copyright notices, attribution notices, or this license from the Software or from copies/forks of it.

